{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will send an angel before you.</b> From here it is proven that until now the holy mind was agreed to the entry of Moses into the land and to bequeathing it to Israel — for even though He said (Exodus 6:1) ״עַתָּה תִרְאֶה״, He nevertheless says ״עֲלֵה״ and so forth, <b>and I will send an angel before you</b> to drive out the seven nations. Or it may be that because he gave his soul for Israel in the incident of the golden calf, the decree of ״עַתָּה תִרְאֶה״ and so forth was annulled."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:17.574639310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}